I read it this was as well.

> Now my turn to be a newbie. If you wear a [ooA that
> changes your alignment to that of the mines town
> altar, can you do water sacrifices and such (hold
> sacfests, come to that) without penalty from your
> own god or your quest leader (once you uncurse and
> take off the [ooA), snagging massive benefits from a
> deluded enemy god?

Yes, you can do this.  Every time you change alignment for any reason
(including putting on or taking of the helm) you will lose any
intrinsic protection, but I see no other negative consequences.  Your
prayers/sacrifices will be to the "correct" god at the time, and when
you remove the [oOA you'll become eligible for your Quest again.


